---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who runs the numbers here, and how."
	pubDate={new Date('September 04 2026')}
>
	<p>
		I'm Carmine. I live in Zurich, I work in analytics, and I lead a small team of data
		analysts by day. Outside work I run marathons, race HYROX, have a soft spot for
		backyard ultras, and coach a running club. I do my admin in Italian, English and
		German, usually in that order of confidence.
	</p>
	<p>
		This blog exists because I kept running the same kind of analysis on my own life
		and never writing it down. What a late hard session does to that night's HRV. What
		a franc buys you in protein at Migros versus McDonald's. Whether a taper actually
		shows up in resting heart rate or only in my head. If it can be measured, it ends up
		in a spreadsheet, and the spreadsheets that turn out to say something end up here.
	</p>
	<p>
		Some posts are about the numbers. Some are about the tools I needed to get at
		them, because the data was sitting in an app with no export button. Both count.
	</p>
	<p>
		A note on how things get made. I run a personal Claude Code setup that handles a
		lot of my admin and side projects. Some of the tools described here were written by
		it under my direction, and some posts start as its draft of a conversation we had.
		Where that is the case the post says so. Everything published is read, checked and
		signed off by me, and the mistakes are mine.
	</p>
	<p>
		No newsletter, no schedule. I write when something is genuinely figured out, which
		is once or twice a month at most. If a post is useful to you, or wrong, the best
		place to tell me is
		<a href="https://github.com/ragonc">GitHub</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>

